<title>CONGO: French troops to reinforce Kinshasa embassy.</title>
<headline>French troops to reinforce Kinshasa embassy.</headline>
<dateline>BRAZZAVILLE 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six French patrol boats left Congo's capital Brazzaville for Zaire's capital Kinshasa across the Zaire River and French military officials said on Saturday they would reinforce the ambassador's residence there.</p>
<p>&quot;We are sending reinforcements to the ambassador's residence,&quot; a military spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>U.S., French, British, Belgian and Portuguese troops were on standby in Congo's capital Brazzaville to evacuate foreign nationals from Kinshasa if need be.</p>
</text>
